When a stored response is revalidated with a 304, Ladybird now counts
its age from the revalidation request, recording that request’s time and
the time of its response in the cache index. Chromium does the same:
HttpCache::Transaction::DoUpdateCachedResponse() sets the cached
response’s request_time and response_time to those of the 304. This
comes from reading Chromium’s source; Gecko and WebKit weren’t checked.
